{
  "dom_id": "step-e5670",
  "name": "Example: Simplifying a Variable Expression Containing a Quotient With Many Factorials",
  "problem": "Given that $k \\geq 1$ is an integer, simplify $\\dfrac {k^2(k - 1)!} {k!}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we notice that \n\n$$\nk! = k \\cdot (k-1)!\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify the numerator as follows:\n\n$$\nk^2 (k-1)! = k \\cdot \\underbrace{k \\cdot (k-1)!}_{k!} = k \\cdot k!\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel the $k!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac {k^2(k - 1)!} {k!} \n&= \\dfrac {k \\cdot k!} {k!}\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {k \\cdot \\cancel{k!}} {\\cancel{k!}} \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac {k} {1} \\[5pt]\n&= k\n\t}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
